{"id":"mahabharata-12-325","work":"mahabharata","part":12,"partName":"शान्तिपर्व","partNameEn":"Shanti Parva","unit":325,"title":"पञ्चविंशत्यधिकत्रिशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 325 · Narada's hymn at the White Island","summary":{"en":"Narada, reaching the great White Island, sees the white men shining like the moon, and bows to them. With raised arms he sings a hymn of many names to the Lord, who is without qualities, the witness of the worlds, the knower of the field and the infinite.","kn":"ಶ್ವೇತ ಮಹಾದ್ವೀಪ ತಲುಪಿದ ನಾರದ ಚಂದ್ರನಂತೆ ಹೊಳೆಯುವ ಬಿಳಿ ಜನರನ್ನು ಕಂಡು ನಮಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಕೈ ಎತ್ತಿ ನಿರ್ಗುಣ, ಲೋಕಸಾಕ್ಷಿ, ಕ್ಷೇತ್ರಜ್ಞ, ಅನಂತನಾದ ಭಗವಂತನಿಗೆ ಅನೇಕ ನಾಮಗಳ ಸ್ತೋತ್ರ ಹಾಡುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"श्वेत महाद्वीप पहुँचकर नारद चन्द्रमा जैसे चमकते श्वेत पुरुषों को देखकर नमन करते हैं। भुजाएँ उठाकर वे निर्गुण, लोकसाक्षी, क्षेत्रज्ञ और अनन्त प्रभु का अनेक नामों वाला स्तोत्र गाते हैं।","te":"శ్వేత మహాద్వీపం చేరిన నారదుడు చంద్రునిలా మెరిసే తెల్లని మనుషులను చూసి నమస్కరిస్తాడు. చేతులెత్తి నిర్గుణుడు, లోకసాక్షి, క్షేత్రజ్ఞుడు, అనంతుడైన ప్రభువుకు అనేక నామాల స్తోత్రం పాడతాడు.","ta":"வெண்தீவை அடைந்த நாரதர் நிலவு போல் ஒளிரும் வெள்ளை மனிதரைக் கண்டு வணங்குகிறார். கைகளை உயர்த்தி குணமற்ற, உலகின் சாட்சியான, வயலை அறிபவனான, முடிவற்ற இறைவனுக்குப் பல பெயர்களைக் கொண்ட துதியைப் பாடுகிறார்.","ml":"മഹത്തായ ശ്വേതദ്വീപിലെത്തിയ നാരദൻ, ചന്ദ്രനെപ്പോലെ തിളങ്ങുന്ന വെളുത്ത മനുഷ്യരെ കാണുകയും അവരെ നമസ്കരിക്കുകയും ചെയ്യുന്നു. കൈകൾ ഉയർത്തി അദ്ദേഹം ഗുണങ്ങളില്ലാത്തവനും ലോകസാക്ഷിയും ക്ഷേത്രജ്ഞനും അനന്തനുമായ ഭഗവാന് അനേകം നാമങ്ങളാൽ ഒരു സ്തുതിഗീതം പാടുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 12.325; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Jun 16 2021","sections":[{"title":"मोक्षधर्मपर्व","titleEn":"Mokshadharma Parva (Duties for liberation)","verses":[{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"प्राप्य श्वेतं महाद्वीपं नारदो भगवानृषिः ।\nददर्श तानेव नराञ्श्वेतांश्चन्द्रप्रभाञ्शुभान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reaching the great White Island, the blessed sage Narada saw those same white, auspicious men, bright as the moon."}},{"n":2,"text":"पूजयामास शिरसा मनसा तैश्च पूजितः ।\nदिदृक्षुर्जप्यपरमः सर्वकृच्छ्रधरः स्थितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He bowed to them with his head and in his mind and was honored by them in return; wishing to see the god, he stood supremely intent on recitation, bearing every hardship."}},{"n":3,"text":"भूत्वैकाग्रमना विप्र ऊर्ध्वबाहुर्महामुनिः ।\nस्तोत्रं जगौ स विश्वाय निर्गुणाय महात्मने ॥","meaning":{"en":"The great sage, a brahmin, with one-pointed mind and arms raised, sang a hymn to the universal, quality-free, great Self."}},{"text":"नारद उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Narada said:"}},{"n":4,"text":"नमस्ते देवदेव निष्क्रिय निर्गुण लोकसाक्षिन् क्षेत्रज्ञ अनन्त पुरुष महापुरुष त्रिगुण प्रधान ।\nअमृत व्योम सनातन सदसद्व्यक्ताव्यक्त ऋतधामन् पूर्वादिदेव वसुप्रद प्रजापते सुप्रजापते वनस्पते ।\nमहाप्रजापते ऊर्जस्पते वाचस्पते मनस्पते जगत्पते दिवस्पते मरुत्पते सलिलपते पृथिवीपते दिक्पते ।\nपूर्वनिवास ब्रह्मपुरोहित ब्रह्मकायिक महाकायिक महाराजिक चतुर्महाराजिक आभासुर महाभासुर सप्तमहाभासुर याम्य ।\nमहायाम्य संज्ञासंज्ञ तुषित महातुषित प्रतर्दन परिनिर्मित वशवर्तिन् अपरिनिर्मित यज्ञ महायज्ञ ।\nयज्ञसंभव यज्ञयोने यज्ञगर्भ यज्ञहृदय यज्ञस्तुत यज्ञभागहर पञ्चयज्ञधर पञ्चकालकर्तृगते पञ्चरात्रिक वैकुण्ठ ।\nअपराजित मानसिक परमस्वामिन् सुस्नात हंस परमहंस परमयाज्ञिक सांख्ययोग अमृतेशय हिरण्येशय ।\nवेदेशय कुशेशय ब्रह्मेशय पद्मेशय विश्वेश्वर त्वं जगदन्वयः त्वं जगत्प्रकृतिः तवाग्निरास्यम् वडवामुखोऽग्निः त्वमाहुतिः ।\nत्वं सारथिः त्वं वषट्कारः त्वमोंकारः त्वं मनः त्वं चन्द्रमाः त्वं चक्षुराद्यम् त्वं सूर्यः त्वं दिशां गजः दिग्भानो हयशिरः ।\nप्रथमत्रिसौपर्ण पञ्चाग्ने त्रिणाचिकेत षडङ्गविधान प्राग्ज्योतिष ज्येष्ठसामग सामिकव्रतधर अथर्वशिरः पञ्चमहाकल्प फेनपाचार्य ।\nवालखिल्य वैखानस अभग्नयोग अभग्नपरिसंख्यान युगादे युगमध्य युगनिधन आखण्डल प्राचीनगर्भ कौशिक ।\nपुरुष्टुत पुरुहूत विश्वरूप अनन्तगते अनन्तभोग अनन्त अनादे अमध्य अव्यक्तमध्य अव्यक्तनिधन ।\nव्रतावास समुद्राधिवास यशोवास तपोवास लक्ष्म्यावास विद्यावास कीर्त्यावास श्रीवास सर्वावास वासुदेव ।\nसर्वच्छन्दक हरिहय हरिमेध महायज्ञभागहर वरप्रद यमनियममहानियमकृच्छ्रातिकृच्छ्रमहाकृच्छ्रसर्वकृच्छ्रनियमधर निवृत्तधर्मप्रवचनगते प्रवृत्तवेदक्रिय अज सर्वगते ।\nसर्वदर्शिन् अग्राह्य अचल महाविभूते माहात्म्यशरीर पवित्र महापवित्र हिरण्मय बृहत् अप्रतर्क्य ।\nअविज्ञेय ब्रह्माग्र्य प्रजासर्गकर प्रजानिधनकर महामायाधर चित्रशिखण्डिन् वरप्रद पुरोडाशभागहर गताध्वन् छिन्नतृष्ण ।\nछिन्नसंशय सर्वतोनिवृत्त ब्राह्मणरूप ब्राह्मणप्रिय विश्वमूर्ते महामूर्ते बान्धव भक्तवत्सल ब्रह्मण्यदेव भक्तोऽहं त्वां दिदृक्षुः एकान्तदर्शनाय नमो नमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Homage to you, god of gods, actionless, quality-free, witness of the worlds, knower of the field, infinite, Person, great Person, the three-quality primal nature; immortal, ether, eternal, being and non-being, manifest and unmanifest, abode of cosmic order, ancient first god, giver of wealth, lord of creatures, good lord of creatures, lord of plants; great lord of creatures, lord of vigor, lord of speech, lord of mind, lord of the world, lord of the sky, lord of the winds, lord of the waters, lord of the earth, lord of the directions; dwelling of old, priest of Brahma, of Brahma's order, of the great order, of the great kings, of the four great kings, of the Abhasvaras, of the Mahabhasvaras, of the seven Mahabhasvaras, of the Yamas; of the great Yamas, of those with and without consciousness, Tushita, Mahatushita, Pratardana, Parinirmita, Vashavartin, Aparinirmita; sacrifice, great sacrifice, source of sacrifice, womb of sacrifice, embryo of sacrifice, heart of sacrifice, praised in sacrifice, taker of the sacrificial share, bearer of the five sacrifices, performer at the five times, follower of the five nights, Vaikuntha; unconquered, mind-born, supreme master, well-bathed, Hamsa, Paramahamsa, supreme sacrificer, Sankhya and Yoga, resting in nectar, resting in gold; resting in the Veda, in kusha grass, in Brahma, in the lotus, lord of the universe; you are the pervader of the world, you are the world's nature; fire is your mouth, you are the submarine fire, you are the oblation; you are the charioteer, you are the vashat-call, you are Om, you are mind, you are the moon, you are the eye and the first, you are the sun, you are the elephant of the directions, the horse-headed light of the quarters; first of the Trisuparna, five-fire, Trinachiketa, rule of the six limbs, Pragjyotisha, Jyeshthasamaga, bearer of the Samika vow, Atharvashiras, the five great cycles, teacher of the foam-drinkers; Valakhilya, Vaikhanasa, of unbroken yoga, of unbroken enumeration, beginning of the age, middle of the age, end of the age, Akhandala, ancient womb, Kaushika; much-praised, much-invoked, of every form, of endless course, of endless enjoyment, infinite, beginningless, middleless, of unmanifest middle, of unmanifest end; abode of vows, dwelling in the ocean, dwelling of fame, dwelling of austerity, dwelling of Lakshmi, dwelling of knowledge, dwelling of renown, dwelling of Shri, dwelling of all, Vasudeva; of every desire, Harihaya, Harimedha, taker of the great sacrificial share, boon-giver, bearer of the yamas, niyamas, great niyamas, krichchhra, atikrichchhra, mahakrichchhra, and all krichchhra restraints, abiding in the teaching of dharma of withdrawal, performer of the Vedic acts of engagement, unborn, all-pervading; all-seeing, ungraspable, unmoving, of great power, of majestic body, pure, greatly pure, golden, vast, beyond reasoning; unknowable, foremost of Brahman, creator of creatures, destroyer of creatures, bearer of great illusion, Chitrashikhandin, boon-giver, taker of the sacrificial cake portion, whose road is gone, whose thirst is cut; whose doubt is cut, turned back from all sides, of brahmin form, friend of brahmins, of universal form, of great form, kinsman, loving to devotees, god of brahmins, I am your devotee and wish to see you: homage, homage, for the vision of the exclusive devotees.\""}}]}]}